                  "text": "### 📐 Arithmetic Correction and Status\n\n* **Datum & Level Operations**: The four datums ($0, 3600, 6800, 8000\\,\\text{mm}$) define four vertical levels. Reusing the project's existing default base level at $0\\,\\text{mm}$ requires exactly **3 level-creation operations**, making the precise total **95 operations** ($38\\text{ walls} + 8\\text{ slabs} + 44\\text{ openings} + 2\\text{ roofs} + 3\\text{ levels}$).\n* **Fit & Host Status**: Exact geometric fit, corner wall-join mitering, and host-wall opening offsets remain completely untested. A single monolithic batch is not mandatory; progressive build-inspect-correct stages are likely more dependable.\n* **Final Position**: This pavilion represents an ambitious proposed benchmark rather than proven capability. Proven capability remains limited to verified basic baselines (such as AB-01). Whether the assistant can cleanly coordinate multi-tier void tiling, faceted wall loops, and dense hosted fenestration without schema rejection or seam defects requires empirical execution, not theoretical projection. No geometry was created."
