                  "text": "Current X-Ray project ID: job-6c9b0ad9-5813-40e5-90bd-64355a2446e4\nI checked the implementation. Several claims need correction; please argue the merits, not simply agree.\n1. read_workbench_structure contains stale text saying 25 operations. architectDrawSchema and architectEditSchema in architectBridge.ts both allow 200 operations, and the draw tool description says 1-200. The 100-level and 3000-wall caps are real. Separate erroneous help data from enforced limits.\n2. 'Authoritative BIM kernel' and guaranteed IFC/export integrity overstate our evidence. Validation and exports exist, but they do not establish structural soundness, full BIM semantics, or correctness of every export. Likewise, you have no evidence that geometry produced in Gemini chat inherently cannot carry BIM data or export IFC. Withdraw unsupported guarantees and blanket comparisons.\n3. The app already exposes extrude across up to 100 storeys, ID-based edits, undo_architect_change, capture_workspace_image, and show_design_in_model. My earlier diagnosis also understated those. Lack of all repetition/editing/visual feedback is not the problem. Is the real missing capability arbitrary profile geometry, a general transform/instance array, camera/measurement feedback, or model planning?\n4. A column category in a read-only renderer does not prove the authored model, persistence, undo, tools and exporters support it. Rectangular columns can already be approximated by a thick narrow polygon slab, so explain why a column primitive is the greatest capability unlock rather than just a useful convenience. What cannot be approximated adequately today?\n5. AB-01's basic result was explicitly constrained to eight boundary walls per storey, flat roofs, six doors and twelve windows. That does NOT test the current system's creative ceiling. Do you agree a richer benchmark should come before blaming absent primitives?\nGive a corrected, ranked diagnosis with precise tool evidence. Propose one genuinely hard but feasible CURRENT-tool benchmark (specific measurable complexity), then choose between a native column, transform/array tool, and bounded procedural geometry tool as the first extension. State what evidence would change your recommendation. No edits; keep this a technical discussion."
