      "objective": "Daniel asks: What is actually stopping you from making something extremely difficult and visually sophisticated in X-Ray, when Gemini chat can generate much more impressive 3D scenes? This is a technical discussion, not an instruction to edit geometry. Inspect your actual exposed tools and read the workbench structure if needed. Separate: (1) hard schema/engine limitations, (2) things you CAN do now but that are laborious, (3) prompt/workflow or visual-quality shortcomings, (4) claims you cannot verify. Name exact tools and operations supporting your answer. Do not use absent source calibration, professional sign-off, or an unmounted workspace as excuses against illustrative creation. Explain your strongest feasible ambitious design with the CURRENT tools and the smallest specific tool addition that would make the greatest difference. Push back if our diagnosis is wrong. No geometry edits, external actions, or invented capabilities.",
